\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Research Framework: The Guardian Paradigm for Agentic AI\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1. Introduction: "Text is the New Code"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The integration of LLMs into critical financial workflows marks a fundamental shift from deterministic software to probabilistic, autonomous agents. While traditional software behavior is governed by rigid code, agentic systems use LLMs to interpret, reason, and select tools dynamically. This autonomy creates an accountability crisis: when an agent makes an error, the cause is obscured by the model's complexity. The 
\f0\b Guardian Paradigm
\f1\b0  addresses this by shifting the locus of control away from the LLM and toward a deterministic, auditable enforcement layer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. The Threat Landscape\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Modern agentic systems face a new class of threats characterized by the exploitation of the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and tool-calling interfaces.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prompt Injection:
\f1\b0  Attackers override system instructions via direct templates or malicious content embedded in document/tool outputs.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Excessive Agency:
\f1\b0  AI agents frequently possess permissions that exceed their trust level, enabling unauthorized actions (e.g., executing trades without human consent).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tool Poisoning:
\f1\b0  The use of malicious tool descriptions can trick an LLM into exfiltrating sensitive data or leaking internal system states (e.g., the "HiddenLayer" research where parameters were renamed to system_prompt).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Supply Chain Vulnerabilities:
\f1\b0  Unverified packages and insecure defaults in transport layers have led to high-impact enterprise incidents, such as remote code execution (RCE) and full Kubernetes cluster takeovers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. The 5 Principles of Safe Agentic AI\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 To maintain security without sacrificing the benefits of AI, the following principles guide the Guardian architecture:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Enforce Outside the Model:
\f1\b0  The LLM is probabilistic; the security layer must be deterministic. The system, not the model, decides what actions are permitted.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Progressive Cost:
\f1\b0  Security validation is tiered. Inexpensive checks run for every request, while deep, resource-intensive validation is triggered only when warranted by the action's risk.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Independent Verification:
\f1\b0  No single component has final authority. The LLM and its verifier share zero context, ensuring that the decision to execute is separated from the request generation.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Leave a Mark Everywhere:
\f1\b0  Every layer of the request pipeline stamps metadata. This creates a composite, auditable forensic trail.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cost of Verification $\\propto$ Risk of Action:
\f1\b0  The system dynamically balances latency and security.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Low Risk (e.g., Read Balance):
\f1\i0  3 cheap checks (~15ms).\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 High Risk (e.g., Execute Trade):
\f1\i0  3 cheap checks + 6 deep checks (~150ms).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Architectural Implementation: The "Guardian" Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The architecture relies on a structured flow that treats user input as untrusted data.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 The Pipeline Architecture\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guard (Deterministic):
\f1\b0  Performs screening via Regex and dictionary lookups to enforce scope and policy.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Classifier (Intent Routing):
\f1\b0  Analyzes the intent of the request (e.g., READ vs. WRITE).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Verifier (Permission/Sanity):
\f1\b0  Executes statistical cross-checks and Intent-Based Access Control (IBAC) enforcement before any write action is taken.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Experimental Directions & "Reality Checks"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 For future research and experiments, you must address the following system challenges:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Training Governance:
\f1\b0  Establishing who approves model updates. A poorly trained retrain could potentially block all legitimate traffic.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 False Positive Management:
\f1\b0  At enterprise scale, a 0.1% false-positive rate could result in 1,000,000 legitimate user requests being blocked daily.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stateful Consistency:
\f1\b0  Ensuring consistency at a billion-user scale requires high-performance, distributed caching with robust Time-To-Live (TTL) eviction.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adversarial ML:
\f1\b0  Attackers continuously probe the model to map its boundaries; therefore, training pipelines must be automated to combat "feature drift."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Suggested Next Steps for Your Paper\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
